 "problems": [
  "talpur-dynasty is a Cliopatria row (1820-1894) owned by a sibling part of sa-05; I drafted a dossier before finding that and did not publish it (draft was in my scratch directory only); kalhora-dynasty cites the same Talpur dynasty page.",
  "The gorkha-kingdom Cliopatria row ends in 1787, but the nepal dossier carries the conquests of Kumaon (1791) and Garhwal (1804); garhwal-kingdom and kumaon-kingdom therefore name nepal as counterpart.",
  "Maratha confederacy members (gwalior, indore, baroda, nagpur, kolhapur, bhopal 1737-1818, jhansi) lie inside the maratha-empire Cliopatria shape until 1818; rendering must treat them as sub-units or tints.",
  "sources_total (94) counts source entries per dossier; 76 distinct pages were opened. Pages that loaded but were unusable (Conquest_of_Sindh, Pratap_Singh_Naruka, Pratap_Singh_Prabhakar, Qudsia_Begum) are not cited.",
  "Validator warnings that remain are counterpart slugs without a dossier yet (matsya-union, vindhya-pradesh, madhya-bharat, travancore-cochin, rampur-state, gohad-state, gond-kingdom-of-deogarh, venad) and one intended empty keyframe: garhwal-kingdom_1804 (the 1804-1814 Gorkha occupation has no land by design).",
  "kutch: the gazetteer region Kutch includes the Great Rann (62,000 km2 against the 19,725 km2 of the 1901 page), so cutch-state uses a polygon cut to India; bhopal-state and rewa-state use hand polygons sized to the page area.",
  "Events with no land on the page are not ledger events: bhopal 1724 cession to the Nizam and jaisalmer 1762 fort recovery are recorded in wars and notes only.",
  "Earlier dossiers were revised after adding pages: gwalior-state (1861 Jhansi gain) and rohilkhand-state (1742 Kumaon parganas gain and a second keyframe) now agree with jhansi-state and kumaon-kingdom.",
  "The network mount is shared: all my writes used a copy plus validate; no temporary files were left in history/. No hearthbot tool or subagent was used."
 ]
}